WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.400 --> 00:06.401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:06.411 --> 00:08.400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

4
00:08.430 --> 00:09.950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

5
00:10.000 --> 00:11.501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

6
00:11.511 --> 00:12.890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

7
00:12.899 --> 00:13.900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

8
00:13.911 --> 00:14.912
[or any particular group of people.]

9
00:15.112 --> 00:17.680
- Ta! - Your sister died under suspicious circumstances.

10
00:17.700 --> 00:19.120
We have to report this to the police.

11
00:19.267 --> 00:21.520
And let the forensic experts determine the cause of her death.

12
00:21.558 --> 00:23.240
Ta didn't want me to tell anyone about this.

13
00:23.250 --> 00:24.320
I'll investigate it myself.

14
00:24.576 --> 00:26.320
Is it possible that your sister might have...

15
00:26.992 --> 00:28.321
maybe she really did take her own life.

16
00:28.534 --> 00:31.050
The only way to find out what happened to Ta

17
00:31.070 --> 00:32.560
is for me to become her.

18
00:33.142 --> 00:34.320
Please don't disappear on me again.

19
00:35.030 --> 00:36.683
And how's the baby?

20
00:37.680 --> 00:38.920
- Ta? - I had a miscarriage.

21
00:39.894 --> 00:40.895
I lost the baby.

22
00:40.923 --> 00:43.280
It's okay. I won't let this happen again.

23
00:43.419 --> 00:44.420
And as for you,

24
00:44.838 --> 00:47.600
get a contraceptive implant so you won't get pregnant again.

25
00:48.176 --> 00:50.250
Hong, who pushed me down the stairs?

26
00:50.395 --> 00:52.000
Here's what happened.

27
00:52.248 --> 00:54.254
Mutta, where did you get that ring?

28
00:54.403 --> 00:55.680
Someone gave it to me.

29
00:56.547 --> 00:58.800
Jenphop proposed to me with that ring.

30
00:58.824 --> 01:00.000
How could you possibly have the same ring?

31
01:00.040 --> 01:01.560
If word of this ever gets out,

32
01:01.680 --> 01:02.920
I'll make every last one of you pay!

33
01:04.078 --> 01:06.920
When it comes to mistresses, there's no level I won't stoop to!

34
01:07.771 --> 01:08.772
Ta!

35
01:10.358 --> 01:12.739
- Are you okay? - If you don't stay away from my husband,

36
01:12.776 --> 01:14.130
I'll make sure you suffer again!

37
01:15.448 --> 01:17.680
I simply got rid of something that had been bothering me.

38
01:18.254 --> 01:19.480
You hurt my sister!

39
01:19.752 --> 01:20.880
You bitch, Nopnapha!

40
01:24.059 --> 01:25.060
Ta.

41
01:25.955 --> 01:27.880
How's the wound from your fall down the stairs?

42
01:28.414 --> 01:29.415
Has it healed yet?

43
01:29.992 --> 01:31.103
The scab has fallen off.

44
01:31.240 --> 01:33.960
It's just a faint scar. It'll fade soon.

45
01:38.806 --> 01:40.160
I think you should quit your job.

46
01:43.062 --> 01:45.600
I'm afraid you'll run into her at the ministry and get into another fight.

47
01:46.500 --> 01:48.531
And you'll have to put up with all the gossip, too.

48
01:49.976 --> 01:52.160
It's okay. I can handle it.

49
01:57.011 --> 01:58.012
Wow.

50
02:00.440 --> 02:01.840
Everything looks so delicious.

51
02:02.486 --> 02:03.760
You're such a good cook.

52
02:06.904 --> 02:09.432
Once we're finally married,

53
02:10.478 --> 02:12.560
I'll get to enjoy your cooking at every meal.

54
02:13.870 --> 02:15.600
I'm definitely going to gain weight, Ta.

55
02:16.248 --> 02:17.249
Would that be so bad?

56
02:18.318 --> 02:20.488
I'm going to fatten up both you and our child.

57
02:21.294 --> 02:22.960
You'll both be nice and chubby.

58
02:23.806 --> 02:24.920
Come on, Ta.

59
02:25.320 --> 02:26.846
Why are you bringing up having kids?

60
02:27.422 --> 02:29.423
Didn't we agree we wouldn't have any children?

61
02:30.600 --> 02:32.691
I'm getting old. I can't handle raising a child.

62
02:35.790 --> 02:37.880
What if we weren't careful?

63
02:43.640 --> 02:44.641
What do you mean?

64
02:49.216 --> 02:50.720
I'm already one month pregnant.

65
02:53.814 --> 02:54.815
What?

66
02:56.155 --> 02:57.156
Are you serious?

67
02:58.000 --> 02:59.001
Director?

68
02:59.600 --> 03:00.601
Director.

69
03:01.075 --> 03:02.250
I love our baby.

70
03:03.902 --> 03:05.440
I want to have a baby with you.

71
03:06.400 --> 03:08.120
Please don't make me have an abortion.

72
03:08.600 --> 03:09.601
Please.

73
03:10.301 --> 03:11.302
Of course not.

74
03:12.126 --> 03:13.880
Ta, listen.

75
03:16.163 --> 03:18.280
If you want to keep the baby, I won't force you to do anything.

76
03:21.126 --> 03:23.250
Ta... Don't worry.

77
03:24.875 --> 03:26.040
I'll take responsibility.

78
03:26.600 --> 03:27.601
Okay?

79
03:31.907 --> 03:32.908
Don't worry, sweetheart.

80
05:04.600 --> 05:05.601
Whoa.

81
05:06.579 --> 05:08.680
I don't even know which part to be shocked about first.

82
05:09.507 --> 05:11.508
Mutta's boyfriend was the director.

83
05:11.806 --> 05:13.880
Then she got pregnant by accident and had a miscarriage.

84
05:15.600 --> 05:17.201
I really have to admire your sister's courage.

85
05:17.500 --> 05:20.501
Of all the men she could've had an affair with, she chose Nopnapha's husband.

86
05:22.000 --> 05:23.001
What's so special about her?

87
05:23.500 --> 05:25.440
I haven't really been following Thai politics.

88
05:26.939 --> 05:29.080
She's done a pretty good job as a minister.

89
05:29.419 --> 05:30.640
Everyone's saying

90
05:30.720 --> 05:32.822
she's going to be the next prime minister.

91
05:33.515 --> 05:36.050
But behind the scenes, she's shady as hell.

92
05:36.200 --> 05:37.550
Her father's a mafia boss,

93
05:37.800 --> 05:40.650
so she's used to pulling strings outside the system to play political games.

94
05:41.400 --> 05:44.560
As for your sister's death, it's obvious who was behind it.

95
05:51.838 --> 05:53.720
The reason Mutta didn't want me telling anyone

96
05:54.318 --> 05:55.800
or digging into the truth

97
05:57.595 --> 05:59.040
was probably because she was afraid I'd get hurt too.

98
06:00.582 --> 06:01.583
You know,

99
06:01.968 --> 06:03.600
I talked to Mutta every single day.

100
06:04.251 --> 06:06.150
Yet I never knew any of this.

101
06:06.702 --> 06:07.703
What the hell...

102
06:08.830 --> 06:10.360
What kind of sister am I?

103
06:11.230 --> 06:12.400
Don't blame yourself, Munin.

104
06:13.187 --> 06:15.320
The reason Mutta kept all this from you

105
06:15.598 --> 06:17.320
was because she didn't want you to worry like this.

106
06:25.118 --> 06:26.850
We grew up in an orphanage.

107
06:29.382 --> 06:30.840
All we had was each other.

108
06:33.707 --> 06:36.180
I thought we were close enough to talk about anything.

109
06:39.760 --> 06:43.161
We even planned to build houses next to each other

110
06:45.430 --> 06:47.200
so we could spend the rest of our lives together.

111
06:49.734 --> 06:51.460
But she kept so many secrets from me.

112
06:56.352 --> 06:58.180
She must've had her reasons.

113
07:02.243 --> 07:03.244
But...

114
07:03.875 --> 07:05.260
I think I've found a flaw in this theory.

115
07:06.819 --> 07:08.820
If Nopnapha really ordered your sister's murder,

116
07:09.368 --> 07:10.800
and you went back to work today,

117
07:10.968 --> 07:12.500
someone as powerful as her would've known, right?

118
07:13.747 --> 07:16.440
If she knew, why hasn't she done anything?

119
07:17.571 --> 07:19.400
Wouldn't she think you're a ghost?

120
07:20.702 --> 07:21.703
Yeah.

121
07:23.155 --> 07:24.520
If she really ordered the murder,

122
07:25.390 --> 07:27.283
why didn't she make sure the body was taken care of?

123
07:28.110 --> 07:29.960
Why leave it in the water for someone to find?

124
07:33.613 --> 07:34.760
Or maybe...

125
07:36.300 --> 07:37.320
she had nothing to do with it after all.

126
07:39.451 --> 07:41.480
Ugh, this is giving me a headache.

127
07:41.835 --> 07:43.880
Can we figure it out later? Let's drink first.

128
07:44.459 --> 07:45.460
Come on, cheers!

129
08:54.966 --> 08:55.967
Yes?

130
08:57.824 --> 08:58.825
Tetris

131
09:00.048 --> 09:02.560
Hey, why are you still awake?

132
09:06.227 --> 09:07.360
Come on, now.

133
09:07.720 --> 09:10.600
You don't have to come first in your class this semester.

134
09:10.854 --> 09:12.240
Let someone else have a turn.

135
09:12.998 --> 09:14.360
Has Mom come home yet?

136
09:16.187 --> 09:17.188
Not yet.

137
09:17.366 --> 09:19.120
She has a cabinet meeting today, so she'll probably be home late.

138
09:20.080 --> 09:22.120
You go ahead and get some sleep.

139
09:25.795 --> 09:26.796
Sweet dreams.

140
09:27.550 --> 09:28.551
Daddy loves you.

141
09:36.152 --> 09:37.153
Night-night.

142
09:41.920 --> 09:43.170
We are dating.

143
09:47.982 --> 09:48.983
So she's back.

144
09:49.683 --> 09:50.760
Have you seen her yet?

145
09:53.102 --> 09:54.360
You've got quite a nose for trouble.

146
09:55.128 --> 09:56.250
Just like a dog.

147
09:58.648 --> 10:00.520
Well, when you've got a womanizing husband, you have to stay alert.

148
10:03.056 --> 10:04.057
How is she doing?

149
10:06.576 --> 10:07.577
She lost the baby.

150
10:13.419 --> 10:14.420
I've never seen a woman smile so wickedly

151
10:15.000 --> 10:17.920
after hearing that someone had a miscarriage.

152
10:20.059 --> 10:21.120
If she died,

153
10:22.400 --> 10:24.401
I'd have an even bigger smile on my face.

154
10:34.942 --> 10:37.440
Fire her tomorrow so we won't have any more problems.

155
10:38.000 --> 10:39.600
What other problems could there be?

156
10:40.568 --> 10:42.250
I've already made her get a contraceptive implant.

157
10:42.880 --> 10:45.360
I guarantee she won't get pregnant again.

158
10:46.358 --> 10:47.867
I'm not just worried about pregnancy.

159
10:48.240 --> 10:50.400
I don't want any parasites leeching off you, either.

160
10:50.971 --> 10:52.572
Because all the money you let her bleed you dry of

161
10:52.654 --> 10:54.640
- is my money! - So what if it's your money?

162
10:55.438 --> 10:57.039
I'm not firing Mutta.

163
10:57.619 --> 10:59.320
I like having her around. Got a problem with that?

164
11:08.059 --> 11:09.060
Fine.

165
11:23.606 --> 11:24.607
Oshi!

166
11:26.395 --> 11:28.560
I need the men in black to do another job for me.

167
11:29.259 --> 11:30.640
I'll contact them for you, ma'am.

168
11:43.811 --> 11:44.958
Don't dwell on it, okay?

169
11:45.256 --> 11:46.760
Call me anytime if you need anything.

170
11:49.422 --> 11:50.520
My ride's here.

171
11:51.200 --> 11:52.201
I'm off now.

172
11:52.270 --> 11:53.285
Get home safe, okay?

173
11:54.800 --> 11:55.801
Bye-bye.

174
11:59.139 --> 12:00.400
Soi Ari 10, please.

175
12:01.300 --> 12:02.301
See you.

176
12:14.947 --> 12:16.448
Northgate Phahonyothin, right?

177
12:17.230 --> 12:18.231
Yes.

178
12:23.320 --> 12:25.321
I've just got a bit of a cold.

179
12:55.043 --> 12:56.044
Excuse me.

180
12:56.264 --> 12:57.400
This isn't the right way.

181
12:57.920 --> 12:58.921
Where are you taking me?

182
12:59.934 --> 13:01.680
Stop the car right now! Stop!

183
13:02.136 --> 13:03.960
I said stop the car! Stop!

184
13:20.678 --> 13:21.920
Where do you think you're going?

185
13:23.347 --> 13:24.348
Well, well, well.

186
13:27.086 --> 13:28.520
Everybody, please calm down.

187
13:29.087 --> 13:31.840
Whatever this is about, I'm sure we can work something out.

188
13:32.532 --> 13:35.560
You'd better stay away from Mr. Jenphop.

189
13:37.112 --> 13:38.640
Because if you don't,

190
13:39.603 --> 13:41.250
you'll be seeing a lot more of us.

191
13:41.600 --> 13:42.601
How about that?

192
13:43.310 --> 13:46.280
I like them fair-skinned. Come here!

193
13:46.500 --> 13:47.680
- Let go of me! - Stop fighting!

194
13:50.982 --> 13:51.983
Let me go!

195
13:55.600 --> 13:57.160
You've got quite a fight in you, huh?

196
14:03.726 --> 14:05.024
You won't fight anymore?

197
14:23.526 --> 14:24.527
Let me go!

198
14:24.731 --> 14:26.050
How much did she pay you?

199
14:26.186 --> 14:27.560
I'll pay you double.

200
14:30.990 --> 14:33.191
It's not often we get our hands on someone this good.

201
14:34.446 --> 14:35.600
Let us have some fun with you.

202
14:41.664 --> 14:44.200
I won first prize for my Mother's Day essay.

203
14:44.427 --> 14:46.200
The teacher wants me to read it at the morning assembly tomorrow.

204
14:47.206 --> 14:49.407
What did you write? Let me read it.

205
14:50.294 --> 14:53.120
I'll show you the video of my speech tomorrow instead.

206
14:57.126 --> 14:58.127
Come in.

207
15:03.987 --> 15:08.000
Today's mission has been completed, ma'am.

208
15:45.160 --> 15:46.161
I have AIDS!

209
15:48.035 --> 15:49.036
I have AIDS!

210
15:49.171 --> 15:50.320
Don't try to fool me.

211
15:51.638 --> 15:52.800
I'm his mistress.

212
15:53.126 --> 15:55.320
How many men do you think I've slept with, huh?

213
15:55.515 --> 15:56.740
Go ahead and try me if you want.

214
16:01.910 --> 16:04.700
Tell whoever hired you that you got the job done.

215
16:05.275 --> 16:07.520
I'll play along. Got it?

216
16:08.320 --> 16:09.960
This is getting way out of hand, Munin.

217
16:10.520 --> 16:11.921
You need to go to the police right now.

218
16:11.974 --> 16:14.080
About both what happened to you and your sister.

219
16:14.982 --> 16:17.014
Nopnapha has way too much power.

220
16:17.223 --> 16:18.918
Even if I report it, the police won't do a thing.

221
16:22.782 --> 16:25.500
Then you need to stay out of this and fly back to America.

222
16:26.334 --> 16:27.896
Go back to your life over there.

223
16:28.270 --> 16:30.560
Don't throw your life away here. It's not worth it.

224
16:30.947 --> 16:31.948
No.

225
16:32.408 --> 16:33.960
I've only been pretending to be Mutta for one day,

226
16:34.024 --> 16:36.000
and I've already been through so much hell.

227
16:36.355 --> 16:37.971
Mutta had been living like this for so long.

228
16:38.472 --> 16:39.960
God knows what she must've gone through.

229
16:43.240 --> 16:44.641
I have to avenge her.

230
17:28.520 --> 17:30.000
[Mr. Sornchai Khoksamroeng (Khem)]

231
17:42.021 --> 17:43.360
Hello, Sornchai.

232
17:44.331 --> 17:45.640
I have a job for you.

233
17:46.520 --> 17:47.824
Who do you want me to take care of?

234
17:48.336 --> 17:50.203
A debtor? A creditor?

235
17:50.811 --> 17:51.812
A mistress?

236
17:52.510 --> 17:53.520
Or a wife?

237
17:55.336 --> 17:56.520
My job is much simpler than that.

238
17:57.363 --> 17:58.840
Just tell me

239
17:59.496 --> 18:00.800
who hired you yesterday.

240
18:01.118 --> 18:02.119
Shit!

241
18:02.520 --> 18:03.521
Sit down.

242
18:05.958 --> 18:07.000
See that woman over there?

243
18:07.616 --> 18:08.617
She's a friend of mine.

244
18:09.104 --> 18:10.422
An undercover cop.

245
18:10.896 --> 18:12.400
She can call for backup at any moment.

246
18:19.899 --> 18:20.912
Tell me who hired you.

247
18:21.424 --> 18:23.245
I want proof of who hired you.

248
18:25.264 --> 18:26.265
I don't know.

249
18:27.520 --> 18:28.920
I get my jobs through an agency.

250
18:29.344 --> 18:30.763
I never deal with the clients directly.

251
18:31.990 --> 18:33.250
Then give me the agency's number.

252
18:35.384 --> 18:37.520
I don't have the agency's number or the client's.

253
18:38.675 --> 18:41.065
They use burner phones to arrange these jobs.

254
18:41.566 --> 18:42.920
Once the job's done, they destroy the phones.

255
18:43.870 --> 18:45.320
There's no way you'll track any of them down.

256
18:45.371 --> 18:47.480
- There has to be a way! - I told you, there isn't!

257
18:47.520 --> 18:50.240
You'd better talk, or I'll let the police question you.

258
18:56.216 --> 18:57.217
You bitch!

259
19:02.472 --> 19:03.570
Well, there is one way.

260
19:04.854 --> 19:06.855
From the moment a job starts until it's completed,

261
19:07.675 --> 19:10.600
the agency uses this phone to coordinate everything.

262
19:11.312 --> 19:13.560
If you want to investigate, that's your window.

263
19:22.907 --> 19:23.908
What?

264
19:23.908 --> 19:25.920
You're seriously going to take down Minister Nopnapha?

265
19:26.091 --> 19:27.300
Have you lost your mind?

266
19:27.700 --> 19:30.040
Yeah, maybe I have.

267
19:30.491 --> 19:31.960
But she killed my sister.

268
19:32.315 --> 19:33.961
So I'm going to make her life a living hell.

269
19:34.518 --> 19:36.960
I'll expose all the evidence of her crimes

270
19:37.131 --> 19:38.380
for the whole country to see.

271
19:39.531 --> 19:41.300
And how are you going to get the evidence?

272
19:41.478 --> 19:44.340
That thug said they destroy everything once the job is done.

273
19:45.576 --> 19:47.400
I'll make them send someone to attack me again.

274
19:47.710 --> 19:49.262
That's when we'll get our evidence.

275
19:49.672 --> 19:51.650
The only way to lure a tiger out of its den

276
19:52.131 --> 19:53.440
is to provoke it until it gets angry

277
19:53.550 --> 19:54.960
and comes charging out so we can catch it.

278
19:56.638 --> 19:59.440
I'm afraid it'll tear you apart before you can catch it.

279
19:59.640 --> 20:01.120
Look what happened to your sister.

280
20:01.288 --> 20:03.432
You're dealing with one of the most powerful people in the country.

281
20:04.611 --> 20:06.360
That's why we need to prepare carefully.

282
20:08.104 --> 20:09.523
And how are you going to provoke her

283
20:09.726 --> 20:11.534
into sending someone after you again?

284
20:12.963 --> 20:15.400
I'll do exactly what Mutta did.

285
20:15.500 --> 20:17.801
There's no need to worry about the budget we've spent.

286
20:18.078 --> 20:19.640
Because we will ensure

287
20:19.659 --> 20:22.040
that every taxpayer's money is put to the best possible use,

288
20:22.080 --> 20:25.120
in keeping with our ministry's motto:

289
20:25.366 --> 20:26.670
- Honesty. Transparency. - [Mrs. Nopnapha Jetsadaphiban]

290
20:26.680 --> 20:28.105
- Fiscal discipline. - [Minister of Digital Finance]

291
20:38.544 --> 20:40.720
I'll become the new Mutta for you.

292
21:00.166 --> 21:01.167
Hello there.

293
21:01.600 --> 21:02.801
Nopnapha.

294
21:17.886 --> 21:18.887
Veekit.

295
21:20.424 --> 21:21.425
Veekit.

296
21:23.571 --> 21:24.572
Veekit!

297
21:25.900 --> 21:26.901
Whoa!

298
21:27.390 --> 21:28.391
Did you change your hairstyle?

299
21:29.208 --> 21:30.209
You look different.

300
21:30.296 --> 21:32.700
Yeah, I felt like becoming a new person.

301
21:34.286 --> 21:37.360
I came to apologize for what I said the other day.

302
21:37.840 --> 21:39.360
After all those insults, why bother apologizing?

303
21:40.486 --> 21:41.600
Come on, let me apologize.

304
21:42.096 --> 21:43.414
I got the wrong idea about you.

305
21:44.091 --> 21:45.240
And that was just a little misunderstanding?

306
21:45.328 --> 21:46.680
You even called me an alpaca.

307
21:47.166 --> 21:48.900
If it had been a big one, would you have called me a macaque?

308
21:53.112 --> 21:54.250
So what did you misunderstand?

309
21:57.100 --> 21:58.101
I...

310
21:58.566 --> 21:59.680
Something bad happened to me.

311
22:00.118 --> 22:01.126
And I thought you were behind it.

312
22:01.216 --> 22:03.720
Something bad? What happened? Who did it?

313
22:06.600 --> 22:07.640
Don't worry about me.

314
22:08.382 --> 22:09.600
I'm fine, really.

315
22:10.179 --> 22:11.960
Anyway, I know who did it now.

316
22:12.510 --> 22:13.511
I'll deal with it myself.

317
22:13.544 --> 22:15.811
Come on, Ta.

318
22:15.886 --> 22:16.887
You can't just leave me hanging like that.

319
22:17.027 --> 22:18.628
Aren't you going to tell me who did what to you?

320
22:23.720 --> 22:25.700
You know who I've been having trouble with.

321
22:27.700 --> 22:28.701
Aunt Nopnapha?

322
22:29.900 --> 22:32.120
Why? What did she do to you this time?

323
22:37.363 --> 22:38.840
Even if I told you, there's nothing you could do.

324
22:39.368 --> 22:40.369
Let's just say

325
22:42.307 --> 22:43.440
I'm still alive.

326
22:43.900 --> 22:44.901
Ta.

327
22:45.300 --> 22:47.101
If you don't want Aunt Nopnapha to hurt you again,

328
22:47.800 --> 22:49.320
just stay away from Uncle Jenphop.

329
22:50.192 --> 22:51.193
It's that simple.

330
22:54.032 --> 22:55.080
What if I want her to hurt me?

331
23:02.168 --> 23:03.169
Ta, are you...

332
23:04.820 --> 23:05.821
Ta!

333
23:06.435 --> 23:07.840
Missing me already, Ta? It's still early.

334
23:08.464 --> 23:09.465
Yes, Director.

335
23:09.824 --> 23:12.425
